From: Surface Go Gaming OS
Subject: [PATCH] Define openat2 for older x86-64 toolchain headers

Bootlin's Linux 5.4 headers do not define __NR_openat2. With assume_kernel
set to the shipped Linux 6.12 kernel, safe_openat's fallback is omitted,
so its compile-time ENOSYS stub makes every sandbox bind fail. Supply the
stable native x86-64 syscall number, as utils.c already does for
mount_setattr. Keep RESOLVE_IN_ROOT and RESOLVE_NO_MAGICLINKS unchanged.

--- a/safe_openat.c
+++ b/safe_openat.c
@@ -27,6 +27,13 @@
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <stdint.h>
+
+/* Toolchain headers can predate the kernel selected at configure time. */
+#ifndef __NR_openat2
+# if defined(__x86_64__) && defined(__LP64__)
+#  define __NR_openat2 437
+# endif
+#endif
 #ifndef __set_errno
 #define __set_errno(val) ((errno) = (val))
 #endif
 
